{"id":"word:hebrew:H5703","type":"word","title":"עַד","subtitle":"H5703 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, a (peremptory) terminus , i.e. (by implication) duration , in the sense of advance or perpetuity (substantially as a noun, either with or without a preposition)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to עַד (H5703) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 51 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"עַד (ʻad) means properly, a (peremptory) terminus , i.e. (by implication) duration , in the sense of advance or perpetuity (substantially as a noun, either with or without a preposition) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 28 9."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"עַד","transliteration":"ʻad","pronunciation":"ad","strong":"H5703","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5703","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["וָ/עֶֽד","לָ/עַֽד","עַ֑ד","לָ/עַ֑ד","לָ/עַ֣ד"],"morphs":[["HR/Ncmsa",20],["HC/Ncmsa",15],["HNcmsa",9],["HR",5],["HNcmpc",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, a (peremptory) terminus , i.e. (by implication) duration , in the sense of advance or perpetuity (substantially as a noun, either with or without a preposition)","usage":"eternity, ever(-lasting, -more), old, perpetually, world without end.","full":"H5703. ad I. עַד and וָעֶ֑ד (so always) noun masculine perpetuity (= advancing time, compare Assyrian adû, time at the present times ); — 1 of past time: עַר מִנִּי Job 20:4 ; עד הררי Hab 3:6 ancient mountains (compare עולם 1 ). **so Gen 49:26 (read עַד הַרְרֵי for עַד הוֺרַ֔י ). 2 of future time , לָעַד (usually לָעַ֑ד ) for ever: a. during lifetime, of king Psa 21:7 ; Prov 29:14 ; of others Psa 9:19 ; 22:27 ; Psalm 61:9; Prov 12:19 . b. of things , יֵחָֽצֵב֑וּן בַּצּוּר לָעַד Job 19:24 . c. of continuous existence , of nations, עַד גְּבֶרֶת (of Babylon, compare עולם 2c ) Isa 47:7 (yet see III. עַד II 3 ); anger , לעד Amos 1:11 ; elsewhere עַד עֲדֵי Psa 83:18 ; 92:8 ; Isa 26:4 ; 65:18 . d. of divine existence , עַד שֹׁכֵן Isa 57:15 ; attributes, לָעַד Psa 111:3 ; 111:10 ; 112:3 ; 112:9 ; residence in Zion, עַד עֲדֵי 132:14 ; law of God לָעַד 19:10 ; promise as to dynasty of David, לָעד 89:30 ; עַד עֲדֵי 132:12 ; inheritance of land, לָעַד 37:29 ; continuous relations between God and his people 1Chr 28:9 ; Isa 64:8 ; Micah 7:18 לעד . e. phrases (see עולם 2m ): וָעֶ֑ד (לְ)וְֺלָם Psa 9:6 ; 10:16 ; 21:5 ; 45:7 ; Psalm 45:18; Psalm 48:15; Psalm 52:10; 104:5 ; 119:44 ; 145:1 ; 145:2 ; 145:21 ; Exod 15:18 ; Micah 4:5 ; Dan 12:3 ; לְעוֺלָם לָעַד Psa 111:8 ; 148:6 ; עַד עַדעֿוֺלְמֵי Isa 45:17 . &#8212; 30:8 read ( עַדעֿוֺלָם ) לְעֵד for a witness ᵑ7 ᵑ9 ᵑ6 Ges Ew Di Che Du) for לָעַד ᵑ0 .","rootNote":"from 5710 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 28 9","keyReferences":["1Chr 28 9","2Sam 3 28","Amos 1 11","Dan 12 3","Exod 15 18","Hab 3 6","Isa 9 5","Isa 26 4"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":51,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 28 9","book":"1Chr","chapter":28,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לָ/עַֽד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Sam 3 28","book":"2Sam","chapter":3,"verse":28,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR"},{"reference":"Amos 1 11","book":"Amos","chapter":1,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לָ/עַד֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Dan 12 3","book":"Dan","chapter":12,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וָ/עֶֽד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Exod 15 18","book":"Exod","chapter":15,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וָ/עֶֽד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Hab 3 6","book":"Hab","chapter":3,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַ֔ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Isa 9 5","book":"Isa","chapter":9,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWor